OL,3,GNEWSAMum hopes Strep B vaccine trial
OL,4,Acan save babies across the world
OL,5,
OL,6,FFirst-time mum Menna Hulme remembers
OL,7,Fwhen she had to be given antibiotics
OL,8,Fintravenously during labour to make
OL,9,Fsure she and her baby were safe.
OL,11,FShe was found, five years ago, to have
OL,12,FGroup B Streptococcus (GBS) in her
OL,13,Fpregnancy, an infection that affects
OL,14,Fone in 1,750 babies in the UK and kills
OL,15,Fone a week.
OL,17,FThen while she was expecting her third
OL,18,Fchild, Hulme became the first woman in
OL,19,FEurope to sign up to a vaccine trial,
OL,20,Frun by Prof Will Parry-Smith from Keele
OL,21,FUniversity, in an attempt to mitigate
OL,22,Fthe effects of GBS.
OL,23,APub: 05-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,358,350,200,160,0,100
